            },
            "reviewBody": "First time I had these in St Thomas! I liked it so much I bought a T-shirt with the recipe on it.",
            "datePublished": "2014-07-05T05:01:27.190Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "EKERR19"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is an amazing indulgence! I first tried these in St. Thomas - a restaurant/bar offered samples on the street, and they SO hit the spot in the humid climate - was I ever hooked! Every time we return to the island, we stop in to our favorite bar for a few of these, then I take my hubby jewelry shopping..:-) I like to add some ice to mine to make them more like a milkshake, which is the way they serve them at the Happy Buzzard in St. Thomas. Thanks so much for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-24T12:42:55.230Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yikes! I can't believe I had all of these liquors in my cabinet! What does that say about me?!? I guess that I like a good drink, including this one! I had just enough cream of coconut leftover from coconut poke cake (from this site) to make this drink. It's creamy and refreshing, perfect to serve with a spicy meal. I made 1/2 recipe, which was just right for the two of us. We loved the nutmeg on top too!",
            "datePublished": "2010-01-18T09:05:17.300Z"
          },
